                <pb facs="0447" n="[425]" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg425"/>

                <head>No. 1.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>London journals all demand that United States shall withdraw claims for indirect
                    damages, as not within intention of Treaty. Ministry alarmed. Am exerting myself
                    with hope to prevent anything rash or offensive being done or said by this
                    Government. Evarts here cooperating.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SCHENCK.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
